#! Completion's ABSENCE, re-verified against a prelude that GREW (le08).
#!
#! le07's `requests/completion-byte` pinned an absence: asked in TYPE
#! position, the server offers the locals in scope, the file's functions
#! and all FIFTY reserved keywords — and not one of the seventeen builtin
#! TYPE names. The le08 contract asks whether s137 changed that, and it
#! is the sharpest question this repository could ask of v0.2.5, because
#! s137's whole delta is FIVE NEW NAMES IN `PRELUDE`
#! (`net_listen_with`, `net_wait`, `os_spawn_with`, `net_adopt_listener`,
#! `os_cpus`). A completion surface that offered prelude names would have
#! to move by exactly five items. `completion-byte` re-recorded
#! header-only, so it did not move — and this file is WHY, stated as a
#! measurement on s137's own witness rather than inferred from that.
#!
#! The absence is wider than le07 could see from a file that binds no
#! builtin call. It is not that builtin TYPES are missing from
#! completion; it is that the PRELUDE IS MISSING FROM COMPLETION
#! ENTIRELY. Measured by set intersection against the pin's own
#! `prelude.rs` rather than by reading the item list: of the **90**
#! names in `PRELUDE` and the **17** in `BUILTIN_TYPES`, the call-position
#! answer offers **zero and zero**. `print` is not offered. `net_listen`
#! is not offered, in a document that calls it twice on the lines above
#! the cursor. So the five names s137 added could not have appeared, and
#! the header-only diff on `completion-byte` is explained rather than
#! merely observed.
#!
#! Four positions on `net/wait_readiness.lu`:
#!
#!   34:19  inside `List[int]`'s type argument — TYPE position, where a
#!          type name is the only legal completion. le07's finding
#!          re-measured at the new pin on a different file: keywords and
#!          locals, no `int`, no `byte`, no `str`, no `bool`.
#!
#!   41:18  partway through the NAME `net_wait`, on the line that calls
#!          it — CALL position. This is the s137 question asked directly:
#!          a user typing `net_wa` in a document whose subject is
#!          `net_wait` is offered no `net_wait`, and no other member of
#!          the family either. The whole item list is recorded, so the
#!          day the prelude reaches completion this record moves by a
#!          knowable amount.
#!
#!   38:44  after the `.` in `net_wait(set, 20)?.len` — the trigger
#!          character the server ADVERTISES in its own
#!          `completionProvider.triggerCharacters: ["."]`, fired on a
#!          `List[int]` that genuinely has a `len`. Empty.
#!
#!   43:12  after the `.` in `woke.len` — the same trigger on a plain
#!          local rather than through a `?`, so the empty answer cannot
#!          be blamed on the error-propagation operator. Also empty.
#!
#! Both dot positions restate le07's second finding at a pin where the
#! member being completed demonstrably exists. Every record here is a
#! regression witness pointed the right way: red-flag shapes, committed
#! so that fixing them shows up as a diff instead of being silently
#! absent. Filed upstream with le07's two.
name      requests/completion-s137
profile   minimal

initialize
open      net/wait_readiness.lu
wait      diagnostics net/wait_readiness.lu
req       completion net/wait_readiness.lu 34:19
req       completion net/wait_readiness.lu 41:18
req       completion net/wait_readiness.lu 38:44 .
req       completion net/wait_readiness.lu 43:12 .
shutdown
